        <lg><l><rs type="place" ana="corpusmd:named_reference" ref="db:4411">dben gnas snar thang <choice><sic>rtsug</sic><corr>gtsug</corr></choice> lag khang mchog</rs> tu ||</l> <l><rs type="person" ana="corpusmd:named_reference" ref="db:4052">mnyaM med bla ma sangs rgyas skyo ston</rs> la || ||</l> <l><lb edRef="inst:4844" n="6b6"/> <rs type="person" ana="corpusmd:named_reference" ref="db:6458">btsun pa ze ston chos <choice><orig>‹kyi›</orig><reg>kyi</reg></choice> rgyal mtshan</rs> gyis ||</l> <l>dad nas zhus shing phyag dpe dngos la <expan>bris so</expan> ||</l></lg> <note type="editorial">We understand that bTsun pa Ze ston requested the teaching from sKyo ston and made a copy, based on a "master copy" that could well have been owned by sKyo ston.</note></seg>
         </ab>
